// error
// SPEC §10.5, #6232: the synthesised member is written in terms of `Json`
// and `JsonEntry`, which the compiler resolves itself -- but only by
// extending an import this module already has from "std/json", and this
// module has none. Reported ONCE, naming the fix, INSTEAD of synthesising --
// a member emitted here would produce a cascade of undefined-name errors on
// a method the user never wrote, every one of them pointing at the class
// header.
@json class User {
  id: i64,
}

fn main() {
  print("${User{ id = 1 }.id}\n")
}
